<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6170" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calcārĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		2. calx, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to lime</i>,
				<i>lime-</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fornax,</span>”
				<i>a limekiln</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 38, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 17, 9, 6, §
			53</span></i>.— Also <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calcārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f. (sc. fornax), <i>a
				lime-kiln</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de calcariā in carbonariam pervenire,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Carn. Christ. 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> (Sc.
			fodina.) <i>A lime-quarry</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 48, 19, 8, §
			10</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calcārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a
			limeburner</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
		16</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
